|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Mayonnaise|mayonnaise]]\n* ¼ cup (120 ml) plain [[Cookbook:yoghurt|yoghurt]]\n* ½ cup (120 g) [[Cookbook:Walnuts|walnuts]], chopped\n* ½ cup (120 ml) condensed cream of [[Cookbook:Mushroom_Soup|mushroom soup]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Hard Boiled Eggs|hard boiled eggs]], peeled and chopped\n* 1 tablespoon chopped fresh [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Lemon_Juice|lemon juice]]\n* 1 ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]] or less, to taste\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* ¼ teaspoon dry [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (700 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]], cooled\n* 2 cups (480 g) cooked [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]], cooled and [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* ¼ cup (60 g) [[Cookbook:Grating|grated]] [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Green_Onion|green onion]], chopped\n* ½ cup (120 g) [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]], chopped\n\n== Procedure ==\n# In the serving bowl, whisk or mix mayonnaise, yoghurt, cream of mushroom soup, lemon juice, salt, pepper, and dry mustard until smooth.\n# Add remaining ingredients and mix well using a spoon or fork.\n# Refrigerate for at least half an hour.\n# Top with a sprig of parsley and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes for salad]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Canadian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hard-cooked egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery root]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mayonnaise]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard powder]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chicken Rice Salad","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup (120 ml) mayonnaise","sourceText":"½ cup (120 ml) mayonnaise","amountText":"½ cup (120 ml) mayonnaise